"how_value_is_captured": "Deere captures value by pricing tractors above functional competitors, leveraging its brand and design to justify the premium, and by selling through dealers who can frame the purchase as a lifestyle choice rather than a purely functional",
"assumptions": ["Suburban homeowners in 1962 have disposable income to afford a premium consumer product.", "Deere can design a tractor that is visually appealing and differentiates from functional competitors.", "Dealers can communicate the status and lifestyle aspects effectively to buyers."], "predictions": ["If Deere introduces a consumer‑focused lawn and garden tractor with distinctive design and branding, purchase intent among suburban homeowners will be higher than for a functionally identical but unbranded competitor.", "Surveys will rank \"status\" and \"modern design\" as top purchase drivers for the Deere tractor."]}}
